// voice.c — High‑Performance rewrite
// Goals:
//  - Preserve the public API and external usage
//  - Fix release-time shortening (time-based envelopes)
//  - Scale to 300k+ voices via worker-local freelists, flat active arrays, precomputed params
//  - SIMD-friendly inner loop, no powf/sqrtf inside the per-sample hot path
//  - Reduced atomics/locks in the render path
//  - Efficient event queues and sustain semantics; pitch bend, CC10/7/11/64 supported
//  - IMPROVED: O(1) voice stealing with no iteration during note-on events
//
// Bug fixes applied (see comments marked FIX throughout):
//  1. NOTE-OFF ROUTING: note-offs now go to the main event queue first; overflow is a
//     true spill path. Old code sent ALL note-offs to overflow (bypassing the main queue),
//     causing a full block of latency and silent drops when overflow filled -> channel panic.
//  2. NOTE_OFF_OVERFLOW_QUEUE_SIZE: increased from 32768 to 524288 for black MIDI loads.
//  3. keyqueue_apply_noteoff_cutoff fast-tail: changed erroneous 'break' on newer voices to
//     'continue', allowing older voices behind a newer one to be reached. The break caused
//     entire chains of note-offs to be silently skipped.
//  4. process_note_off_event: added early-return when off_order >= on_order to avoid
//     releasing voices with no matching note-on (prevents phantom note-offs under VOR merging).
//  5. g_use_fast_note_off_tail: now ON by default. Set SS_FAST_NOTE_OFF=0 to disable.
//  6. channel_release_all_held_voices / channel_all_sound_off / channel_all_notes_off /
//     channel_kill_group: replaced O(max_voices) full-array scans with per-key queue walks.
//     At 1M voices a full scan was stalling the audio thread on sustain-off and CC123.
//  7. Worker freelist refill: reduced per-cycle target from active_cap/4 (up to 4096) to 256.
//     The aggressive drain was starving sibling workers and causing spurious steal cascades.
//
// Build tips:
//  - Compile with /O2 /GL and enable AVX2 if available (/arch:AVX2). SSE2 baseline is fine.
//  - Define VOICEDEBUG for verbose logs.

